{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj3u1HJTspHRbxUKqDuP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*You stand before a plain wooden door, old and weathered. A single iron keyhole glows faintly.*\n\n**CLICK.**\n\n*The tumblers turn. The grain of the wood shivers. A thin line of warm light spills from the widening crack as the door swings slowly inward, hinges groaning with the weight of long stillness.*\n\n*Beyond: a corridor stretching further than it should, lit by candles that burn without flickering. The air smells of old paper and something sweeter — possibility, maybe. Or memory.*\n\n*The door holds itself open. It will not hold forever.*\n\n**You may pass.**"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":145,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}